---
layout: chapter.njk
pageId: reference
subtitle: "Everything you need at the table"
permalink: rules/reference.html
extraHead: |
  <style>
    /* ── Quick Reference Cards ── */
    .ref-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
    }
    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .ref-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }

    .ref-card {
      /* A grid item's automatic minimum is its min-content width, so a long list line
         pushed the card past its track and widened the page at 390px. */
      min-width: 0;
      overflow-wrap: break-word;
      background: var(--bg-surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
      border-radius: 6px;
      padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    }
    .ref-card.full-width {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }

    .ref-card h3 {
      font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      color: var(--theme-accent);
      margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
      padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
      letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    }
    .ref-card h3::after { display: none; }

    .ref-card p, .ref-card li {
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .ref-card ul {
      list-style: none;
      padding: 0;
    }

    .ref-card li {
      padding: 0.15rem 0;
    }

    .ref-card li::before {
      content: '\203A';
      color: var(--theme-accent);
      margin-right: 0.4em;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .ref-formula {
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      color: var(--text-bright);
      background: var(--bg-raised);
      border-radius: 3px;
      padding: 0.15rem 0.4rem;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    /* At phone width a formula cannot stay on one line without dragging the page
       sideways with it, so it wraps at its spaces instead. */
    @media (max-width: 560px) {
      .ref-formula { white-space: normal; }
    }

    .ref-card table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      margin: 0.4rem 0;
    }
    .ref-card th {
      text-align: left;
      font-weight: 600;
      color: var(--text-dim);
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
    }
    .ref-card td {
      padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem;
      color: var(--text);
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.02);
    }
    .ref-card td:first-child {
      font-weight: 600;
      color: var(--text-bright);
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .ref-note {
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      color: var(--text-dim);
      font-style: italic;
      margin-top: 0.3rem;
    }

    .ref-highlight {
      color: var(--galvanic);
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    .ref-aether { color: var(--aether); }
    .ref-galvanic { color: var(--galvanic); }

    /* ── Flowcharts ── */
    .flowchart-section {
      margin: 2rem 0;
    }
    .flowchart-container {
      background: var(--bg-surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
      border-radius: 6px;
      padding: 1.5rem;
      margin: 1rem 0;
      overflow-x: auto;
    }
    /* Stage labels. Each flowchart is three diagrams: whole, neither chart fitted a
       portrait page at any orientation (3:1 and 5:1 top-down, 1:7 and 1:12 across). */
    .flowchart-stage {
      margin: 1.6rem 0 0;
      font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif;
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.18em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--theme-accent);
    }
  </style>
---

    <!-- ══════════════ CORE MECHANICS ══════════════ -->

    <h2 id="core" data-toc="Core Mechanics">Core Mechanics</h2>

    <div class="ref-grid">

      <div class="ref-card">
        <h3>The Roll</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Roll <span class="ref-formula">d100 &le; target</span> = success</li>
          <li><strong>01</strong> = always a critical success</li>
          <li><strong>00</strong> = always a fumble</li>
          <li>Crit range: target only (1&ndash;25), 2 numbers (26&ndash;50), 3 (51&ndash;75), 4 (76&ndash;99), counted down from your target</li>
          <li><strong>Opposed:</strong> both roll, larger margin wins; one success beats one failure</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="ref-card">
        <h3>Skill Targets</h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom:0.4rem;">
          <span class="ref-formula">Target = ((10 + stat) &times; level) + 30</span>
        </p>

    {% spot "notebook", "An operative checks a pocket notebook while walking a busy city street", "center" %}
        <p style="margin-bottom:0.4rem;">
          <span class="ref-formula">Unskilled = (5 + stat) &times; 5</span>
          <span class="ref-formula">Stat check = (5 + stat) &times; 10</span>
        </p>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Stat</th><th>Full Name</th><th>Range</th></tr>
          <tr><td>BR</td><td>Brawn</td><td>&minus;3 to +3</td></tr>
          <tr><td>PC</td><td>Physical Coordination</td><td>&minus;3 to +3</td></tr>
          <tr><td>IN</td><td>Intellect</td><td>&minus;3 to +3</td></tr>
          <tr><td>SP</td><td>Social Prowess</td><td>&minus;3 to +3</td></tr>
          <tr><td>AW</td><td>Awareness</td><td>&minus;3 to +3</td></tr>
          <tr><td>PW</td><td>Power</td><td>&minus;3 to +3</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- ══════════════ DAMAGE & RECOVERY ══════════════ -->

    <h2 id="damage" data-toc="Damage &amp; Recovery">Damage &amp; Recovery</h2>

    <div class="ref-grid">

      <div class="ref-card">
        <h3>Wound Track</h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom:0.3rem;">HP per tier = <span class="ref-formula">7 + BR</span></p>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Tier</th><th>Penalty</th></tr>
          <tr><td>OK</td><td>&mdash;</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Harmed</td><td>&minus;10% to all rolls</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Maimed</td><td>&minus;25% to all rolls</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Incapacitated</td><td>&minus;50% to all rolls</td></tr>
        </table>
        <p class="ref-note">Wound and exhaustion penalties stack.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ref-card">
        <h3>Exhaustion Track</h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom:0.3rem;">EP per tier = <span class="ref-formula">7 + PW</span></p>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Tier</th><th>Penalty</th></tr>
          <tr><td>OK</td><td>&mdash;</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Wearied</td><td>&minus;10% to all rolls</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Drained</td><td>&minus;25% to all rolls</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Overwhelmed</td><td>&minus;50% to all rolls</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="ref-card">
        <h3>Death Saves</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Triggered when reduced below 0 HP in Incapacitated tier</li>
          <li>Every 3 counts, roll <span class="ref-formula">d100</span></li>
          <li>02&ndash;49 = hold &nbsp;|&nbsp; 50&ndash;99 = fail &nbsp;|&nbsp; 3 fails = dead</li>
          <li><strong>01</strong> = stabilize &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>00</strong> = instant death</li>
          <li>Medicine (speed 5) stabilizes &nbsp;|&nbsp; Mend spell heals</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="ref-card">
        <h3>Recovery</h3>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Type</th><th>Rate</th></tr>
          <tr><td>HP (natural)</td><td>1d4 per hour of rest</td></tr>
          <tr><td>HP (medical care)</td><td>1d4 + 1d4 per hour</td></tr>
          <tr><td>EP (natural)</td><td>1d8 per hour of rest</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- ══════════════ SPELLCASTING ══════════════ -->

    <h2 id="casting" data-toc="Spellcasting">Spellcasting</h2>

    <div class="ref-grid">

      <div class="ref-card full-width">
        <h3>Casting Basics</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Each spell has a fixed casting time &rarr; roll <span class="ref-formula">d100</span> against casting target &rarr; tier determined by margin</li>
          <li>Concentration check (if interrupted): <span class="ref-formula">(PW + 4) &times; 10</span></li>
          <li>Cancel a spell: pay &frac12; Weak EP cost, 10% backlash chance (burn only, no wild effect)</li>
        </ul>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Margin Under Target</th><th>Tier Achieved</th></tr>
          <tr><td>1&ndash;10</td><td>Weak</td></tr>
          <tr><td>11&ndash;30</td><td>Standard</td></tr>
          <tr><td>31&ndash;50</td><td>Strong</td></tr>
          <tr><td>51+</td><td>Spectacular</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Over target</td><td>Misfire</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="ref-card">
        <h3>Scholarly Casting</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Roll <span class="ref-formula">1d100</span></li>
          <li>Access to all 6 schools</li>
          <li>Learned spells only (spellbook)</li>
          <li>Can freely choose a lower tier than rolled</li>
          <li>Spells known: <span class="ref-formula">7 + PW</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="ref-card">
        <h3>Wild Casting</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Roll <span class="ref-formula">2d100</span>, use the one farther from target</li>
          <li>+10 bonus to casting target</li>
          <li>Access to selected schools only</li>
          <li>Know all spells in accessible schools</li>
          <li>Limited tier suppression, set by the casting target bracket</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="ref-card">
        <h3>Backlash</h3>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Tier</th><th>Scholarly</th><th>Wild</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Weak</td><td>5%</td><td>10%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Standard</td><td>10%</td><td>15%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Strong</td><td>15%</td><td>20%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Spectacular</td><td>25%</td><td>30%</td></tr>
        </table>
        <p class="ref-note">Checked on every cast (success or misfire). On backlash: 1d4 physical damage + 25% chance of wild effect. Wild effect residue persists until long rest after effect fades.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ref-card">
        <h3>Misfire &amp; Push</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Misfire</strong> (roll over target): pay misfire EP, suffer misfire effect, 0 accumulation</li>
          <li><strong>Push It:</strong> +1 tier; cost = &frac12; current EP + full pushed EP; 2&times; backlash chance</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="ref-card">
        <h3>Aetheric Balance</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Spells shift <span class="ref-aether">Aetheric</span>: +1/+2/+3/+4 by tier</li>
          <li>Galvanic weapons shift <span class="ref-galvanic">Galvanic</span>: &minus;rating per shot (1&ndash;3)</li>
          <li><span class="ref-formula">Eff. Reliability = Base &minus; (net &times; 2)</span></li>
          <li><span class="ref-formula">Eff. Casting = Base + (net &times; 2)</span></li>
          <li>Each side helps its own and hurts the other</li>
          <li>Decays 1 point/min toward zone baseline</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- ══════════════ SPELLCASTING FLOWCHART ══════════════ -->

    <div class="flowchart-section">
      <h3 id="spell-flow" data-toc="Spellcasting Flowchart">Spellcasting Flowchart</h3>

      <h4 class="flowchart-stage">1 &middot; Casting</h4>
      <div class="flowchart-container">
        {% flowplate "spell-1-casting" %}
      </div>

      <h4 class="flowchart-stage">2 &middot; The Roll</h4>
      <div class="flowchart-container">
        {% flowplate "spell-2-roll" %}
      </div>

      <h4 class="flowchart-stage">3 &middot; Backlash</h4>
      <div class="flowchart-container">
        {% flowplate "spell-3-backlash" %}
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ══════════════ COMBAT ══════════════ -->

    <h2 id="combat" data-toc="Combat">Combat</h2>

    <div class="ref-grid">

      <div class="ref-card">
        <h3>Timing Track</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Declare action &rarr; place token at current count + action speed</li>
          <li>Resolve when the count reaches the token</li>
          <li>Declaration order: lowest PC first (best reactions declare last)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="ref-card">
        <h3>Active Defense</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Melee/Brawl/Athletics opposed roll</li>
          <li>Costs +2 speed on your next action</li>
          <li><strong>Parrying</strong> tag: +10% to defense roll</li>
          <li><strong>Shields:</strong> passive soak (Ballistic or Martial)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="ref-card">
        <h3>Armor</h3>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Type</th><th>Stops</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Ballistic soak</td><td>Firearms damage</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Martial soak</td><td>Melee damage</td></tr>
        </table>
        <ul>
          <li>If damage exceeds soak: 25% chance of degradation (&minus;1 soak)</li>
          <li><strong>Crushing</strong> tag: 50% degradation chance</li>
          <li><strong>Hinder:</strong> &minus;5%/pt to PC-based rolls and Athletics; +1 cast speed/pt</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="ref-card">
        <h3>Range &amp; Cover</h3>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Band</th><th>Modifier</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Close</td><td>Melee range</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Near</td><td>No modifier</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Far</td><td>&minus;10%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Distant</td><td>&minus;20%</td></tr>
        </table>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Sprint:</strong> speed 3 to move one band</li>
          <li>Partial cover: &minus;10% &nbsp;|&nbsp; Heavy cover: &minus;20%</li>
          <li>Firing into melee: &minus;10%</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="ref-card full-width">
        <h3>Malfunction</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Always</strong> roll Reliability first (<span class="ref-formula">d100 roll-under</span>), then roll Firearms to hit</li>
          <li><span class="ref-formula">Eff. Reliability = Base &minus; (net balance &times; 2)</span></li>
        </ul>
        <table>
          <tr><th>d10</th><th>Severity</th><th>Effect</th></tr>
          <tr><td>1&ndash;5</td><td>Click</td><td>Weapon doesn&rsquo;t fire, lose action</td></tr>
          <tr><td>6&ndash;7</td><td>Jam</td><td>Weapon jammed, must clear (weapon's reload time)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>8</td><td>Misfire</td><td>Round fires wildly, random direction</td></tr>
          <tr><td>9</td><td>Mechanical Failure</td><td>Weapon needs repair, unusable</td></tr>
          <tr><td>10+</td><td>Catastrophic</td><td>Weapon destroyed, 1d6 damage to wielder</td></tr>
        </table>
        <p class="ref-note">Galvanic weapons: +1 to severity roll.</p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- ══════════════ COMBAT FLOWCHART ══════════════ -->

    <div class="flowchart-section">
      <h3 id="combat-flow" data-toc="Combat Flowchart">Combat Flowchart</h3>

